      "post_id": "87018",
      "author_handle": "Amelia88",
      "date_as_displayed": "Posted 10 years 7 months ago",
      "body": "Did anyone use a doula for their birth? One of my close friends did and really enjoyed the experience - she liked the coaching and calmness that her doula provided. My husband did a great job coaching me so I didn't end up getting a doula to attend my birth, but it seems to be becoming more and more common!\nWhat are your thoughts on doula services?",
      "permalink": "https://www.justparents.co.uk/forums/topic-10061/#87018",
      "raw_file": "_raw/forums-deep/justparents/responses/d12f08d84ab5a8a90f3b.html",
      "page_url": "https://www.justparents.co.uk/forums/topic-10061/",
      "role": "original_post",
      "original_post_id": "87018"
    },
    {
      "post_id": "87104",
      "author_handle": "darkchild",
      "date_as_displayed": "Posted 10 years 7 months ago",
      "body": "I did not use one because I attended antenatal classes at the hospital weekly; were I was registered and most of what to be expected was taught to us.\nI also watched videos on YouTube, did so much research and did some breathing and kegel exercises. It all went well and I don't think I would need one for my next baby.",
      "permalink": "https://www.justparents.co.uk/forums/topic-10061/#87104",
      "raw_file": "_raw/forums-deep/justparents/responses/d12f08d84ab5a8a90f3b.html",
